        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="entra" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Microsoft Entra ID&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;App registration, groups&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;arcSize=12;fillColor=#f7f6f4;strokeColor=#8a8781;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=37;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1460" y="110" width="200" height="80" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="entra-icon" parent="entra" value="" style="shape=image;html=1;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/svg+xml,;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="88.0" y="11" width="24" height="24" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pipeline" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Delivery pipeline&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Azure DevOps, OIDC&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;arcSize=12;fillColor=#f7f6f4;strokeColor=#8a8781;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=37;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1460" y="495" width="200" height="80" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pipeline-icon" parent="pipeline" value="" style="shape=image;html=1;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/svg+xml,;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="88.0" y="11" width="24" height="24" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="email" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Email recipients&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Alert and budget emails&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;arcSize=12;fillColor=#f7f6f4;strokeColor=#8a8781;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=37;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="890" y="850" width="200" height="80" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="email-icon" parent="email" value="" style="shape=image;html=1;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/svg+xml,;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="88.0" y="11" width="24" height="24" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-health" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Health checks and alerts: what they watch and why&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Probes:&lt;/b&gt; GET /healthz on port 8000, sent by the Container Apps platform from inside the environment, as both the liveness and the readiness probe. The request never leaves the private network.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why the platform probes, not a web test:&lt;/b&gt; the app has no public address, so Azure&amp;#x27;s internet availability tests cannot reach it from any region.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why /healthz:&lt;/b&gt; it is the only path excluded from sign-in (authConfigs excludedPaths), so the platform can call it without a token. Every other path redirects to Entra ID.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;What happens on failure:&lt;/b&gt; a failed liveness probe restarts the container; a failed readiness probe takes the replica out of traffic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Alerts:&lt;/b&gt; severity 2 when the container restarts at all within 15 minutes, and severity 2 when more than 5 requests return 5xx within 15 minutes. Both are checked every 5 minutes and email the Action Group.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Traces:&lt;/b&gt; when APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING is set, the app sends OpenTelemetry traces, requests, dependencies, exceptions and logs to Application Insights.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Does not prove:&lt;/b&gt; that users can reach the app over the hub and corporate DNS, or that sign-in works (nothing tests from outside the environment). A replica stuck as not ready raises no alert, because it is not restarted and returns no 5xx." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="950" width="800" height="235" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-plain" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;How users reach the app, and how it reports back&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;What happens&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A user opens the app&amp;#x27;s internal address from the corporate network; the hub and private DNS take them straight to it, never over the internet&lt;br&gt;• Microsoft Entra ID checks that they belong to an allowed group before the app sees the request&lt;br&gt;• Azure checks every few seconds that the app is alive and restarts it if it is not&lt;br&gt;• The app records what it did and any errors in Azure monitoring; restarts and bursts of errors email the team&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why we do it this way&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• The app is for internal users only, so it has no public address at all&lt;br&gt;• Sign-in is handled by Azure, so the app never sees passwords&lt;br&gt;• Any team can bring its own app: it only has to answer on port 8000 and at /healthz" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="860" y="950" width="800" height="235" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-mind" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;What to keep in mind&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hub dependency:&lt;/b&gt; users reach the app only once the platform team completes the hub side (peering, routing and corporate DNS for the environment domain). Agree it before the first apply.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Public egress:&lt;/b&gt; image pulls and telemetry go to public Azure endpoints (Basic registry, no Monitor Private Link), protected by identity and keys. If policy requires private-only traffic, move to a Premium registry and a Monitor Private Link Scope.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sign-in secret:&lt;/b&gt; it rotates every 180 days, but only on the next apply. An environment left unapplied for about 210 days stops signing users in.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zones and replicas:&lt;/b&gt; uat and prod run 2 replicas spread across availability zones (zone_redundancy_enabled, fixed at creation). dev and qa run 1 replica in one zone, so a crash there is a short outage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Request limit:&lt;/b&gt; ingress ends requests after 240 seconds, and the app server may cut them sooner (the example uses a 120 s gunicorn timeout).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cost:&lt;/b&gt; about $35 a month in dev and qa and $67 in uat and prod when mostly idle (up to $109 and $219 if busy all month), at West Europe list prices. Compute is most of it; the Basic registry is $5, or $51 as Premium for zone redundancy. A budget warns at 80 % actual and 100 % forecast." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="1215" width="800" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-why" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Why pick this design, and its trade-offs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Container Apps, not App Service:&lt;/b&gt; runs any image with no App Service plan to size. An internal environment gives private ingress without a separate private endpoint. Trade-off: less control over the runtime than App Service plans; the environment needs its own /27 subnet.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Container Apps, not AKS:&lt;/b&gt; no cluster to run, patch or secure for one small web app. Trade-off: no custom sidecars, operators or cluster add-ons.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Internal load balancer only:&lt;/b&gt; every user is internal, so there is no internet surface to defend. The public variant, with Front Door and WAF, is a separate template. Trade-off: no one off the corporate network can reach it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zone-redundant in uat and prod, not everywhere:&lt;/b&gt; prod keeps serving through a zone failure and uat rehearses it; dev and qa do not need it. Trade-off: fixed at creation, and the second always-on replica costs about $32 a month.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Built-in sign-in, not in-app code:&lt;/b&gt; one Entra setup works for any language, Entra itself enforces the allowed groups, and the app stays generic. Trade-off: fine-grained roles still need code that reads the claims.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Managed identity, not registry passwords:&lt;/b&gt; the admin user is off, so there are no credentials to store or rotate. Trade-off: the pipeline still needs AcrPush through its own service connection.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Basic registry, not Premium:&lt;/b&gt; a private registry needs Premium, which a small workload does not justify. Revisit if policy requires private endpoints. Trade-off: the registry keeps a public endpoint and no geo-replication.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;No storage account:&lt;/b&gt; the app is stateless. Add Blob storage only when it must keep files or run longer than 240 seconds. Trade-off: nothing survives a restart." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="860" y="1215" width="800" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e0" parent="1" value="HTTPS" style="html=1;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;endFill=1;strokeColor=#3f3f52;strokeWidth=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;endArrow=classic;endSize=6;jettySize=auto;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.85;entryY=0;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" source="user" target="hub">
